    <DataNode elementId="INOSITOL-1456-TETRAKISPHOSPHATE" textLabel="D-myo-inositol (1,4,5,6)-tetrakisphosphate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MRVYFOANPDTYBY-YORTWTKJSA-F" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="572.8299560546875" centerY="972.519287109375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco, SRI, caspi">Like several other inositol phosphates, |FRAME: INOSITOL-1456-TETRAKISPHOSPHATE| is a second messenger molecule that plays a critical role in cellular signaling |CITS: [11457089]|. At micromolar concentrations it inhibits IGF-1-induced thymidine incorporation in human breast cancer cells and thus prevents the ability of these cells to grow |CITS: [10834940]|. It is also involved in nuclear processes since it is required for gene regulation and may control gene expression |CITS: [10720331]|.</Comment>
